{"input_tokens":215335,"output_tokens":3798,"requests":7}}],"version":1},"findings":[{"block_threshold":0.9,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Extend the inbound census/Scope to cover `apply_inbound_events._inbound_create_resolve_and_write:76`, wiring `recover_type_label(raw_labels)` to win over the raw issuetype (mirroring the status sibling `_inbound_create_write_status_event:211`), and add an inbound-create round-trip AC; re-derive the `recover_status_label` reference set via find_referencing_symbols to confirm no other consumer is missed.","cohort":["project.symbol-reference-completeness"],"criteria":["project.symbol-reference-completeness"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":0.1,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: 'Inbound: NEW `inbound_fields.recover_type_label` (mirror `recover_status_label` `:152`) + `_LOCAL_TYPE_VOCAB` ... wired at `:311-313`, label-over-raw `:326`.'","grep: `recover_status_label` is consumed at `apply_inbound_events.py:211` (`local_status: str | None = recover_status_label(raw_labels)`), a site NOT covered by the plan's inbound wiring which names only `inbound_fields`.","code: `apply_inbound_events._inbound_create_resolve_and_write:76` sets `ticket_type = _JIRA_TYPE_MAP.get(issuetype, 'task')` from the raw issuetype with `raw_labels` in scope (:82) but no `recover_type_label` call.","Scope list omits `apply_inbound_events.py`."],"finding":"The inbound census for the new `recover_type_label` (mirror of `recover_status_label`) enumerates only the `inbound_fields._map_jira_to_local_fields` wiring, omitting a second inbound consumer. `recover_status_label` — the sibling the plan mirrors — is also called on the inbound-CREATE path at `apply_inbound_events._inbound_create_write_status_event:211`; the corresponding type resolution at `_inbound_create_resolve_and_write:76` (`_JIRA_TYPE_MAP.get(issuetype, 'task')`) never consults the `rebar-type:` label, so the plan's inventory misses this patch site.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f7dd62eb9ca96026e","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Surface-parity census — 'Inbound: NEW inbound_fields.recover_type_label (mirror recover_status_label :152) ... wired at :311-313, label-over-raw :326' and the Scope list (no apply_inbound_events.py)","norm_id":"ncb5c0fb9bd48b2df","priority":1.0,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["apply_inbound_events._inbound_create_resolve_and_write:76 — inbound-create of a Jira issue carrying a lossy `rebar-type:` label resolves ticket_type from the raw issuetype, silently discarding the stamped local type and breaking the round-trip symmetry the plan asserts for the type axis (the STATUS sibling at :211 already honours the label).","apply_inbound_events.py — omitted from Scope, so the patch is never applied and the parity the plan claims with the status axis is only partial."],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"omits_required_site","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Clarify in Finding 4 that the mapper COERCES issuetype via type_map (built-in .get(ticket_type, 'Task') fallback preserved when type_map is None), and that fail-closed fires ONLY in the up-front assert_type_decisions_complete gate — the word 'fail-closed' on steps (4)/(5) is misleading.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.198,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Finding 4: 'outbound_fields._map_local_to_jira_fields (:101) resolves issuetype via type_map (replacing coerce :143), fail-closed; (5) DC _map_local_to_dc_fields (coerce :86) same.'","acli finding: 'Re-resolving via LOCAL_TYPE_TO_JIRA inside acli would fail-close on EVERY differ create (\"Story\" isn't a key).' — issuetype is a coerced NAME, not a re-resolvable raw local type.","Finding 1 (G7) places fail-closed UP FRONT: 'fail-closed fires ONCE UP-FRONT, before the mutation loop' — the mapper is not the fail-closed site.","The seam mirrors status, where the mapper omits-or-drifts rather than raising; issuetype is mandatory on create so it must coerce (built-in .get(ticket_type,'Task')), not raise."],"finding":"Finding 4 describes the field-mapper's issuetype resolution as 'fail-closed', but issuetype is mandatory on create and the plan's own division of labor puts fail-closed ONLY in the up-front gate (Finding 1/G7) while the mapper coerces to a Jira type name.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f72b8e14e307386ad","impact":0.536,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach / Finding 4 (G1G2), steps (4) and (5)","norm_id":"ne822aa5a6abec937","priority":0.402,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Implementer reads 'fail-closed' literally and raises inside the mapper on an undecided/unmapped type, breaking every differ create for a type whose coerced Jira NAME isn't a type_map key."],"severity":"major","suggested_fix":"Reword Finding 4 (4)/(5) to: 'resolves issuetype via type_map, coercing an unmapped type to the built-in Task fallback (fail-closed is enforced up front by assert_type_decisions_complete, not here).'","tier":"LLM","validity":0.75,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"yes","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"medium","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":0.75,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Correct Finding 4's mapper census: the jira/backend.py:73 body is _JiraOutbound (not JiraBackend); enumerate the FOURTH surface — the JiraBackend.map_local_to_remote delegator at jira/backend.py:219 — so type_map is threaded there too.","cohort":["E4"],"criteria":["E4"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.4667,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: 'Add type_map ... to: (1) OutboundMapper Protocol (_backend.py:372); (2) Cloud JiraBackend.map_local_to_remote (jira/backend.py:73, forwards status_map :89); (3) DC (jira_datacenter/backend.py:121)'","search 'class ' in jira/backend.py -> :56 class _JiraOutbound, :188 class JiraBackend; map_local_to_remote at :73 (inside _JiraOutbound) and :219 (inside JiraBackend)","jira/backend.py:232-245: JiraBackend.map_local_to_remote is a 'convenience delegator to the outbound role's CREATE mapper' that forwards status_map=/type_map= into self.outbound.map_local_to_remote","The :73 body belongs to _JiraOutbound, not JiraBackend as the plan labels it"],"finding":"Finding 4's confident enumeration 'thread type_map through ALL THREE OutboundMapper impls' and its label 'Cloud JiraBackend.map_local_to_remote (jira/backend.py:73)' are refuted by Read: jira/backend.py:73 is _JiraOutbound.map_local_to_remote (the role impl), and there is a FOURTH, un-named map_local_to_remote delegator at JiraBackend:219 that forwards status_map/type_map into .outbound. The census of three (Protocol + Cloud:73 + DC:121) omits the JiraBackend:219 delegator, so a literal reading of the plan would miss a live map_local_to_remote signature — the exact TypeError-risk the plan itself flags.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f3c718a54b43ecbe1","impact":0.85,"is_primary":null,"location":"Finding 4 (G1G2) — thread type_map through ALL THREE OutboundMapper impls; jira/backend.py:73 and :219","norm_id":"n0dfd52db6fb57ec6","priority":0.2833,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A caller holding the backend facade calls JiraBackend.map_local_to_remote(..., type_map=...) — if the plan's 3-surface census is implemented literally, the :219 delegator lacks type_map and raises TypeError, the failure mode the plan warns about"],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"In Finding 4, relabel item (2) as '_JiraOutbound.map_local_to_remote (jira/backend.py:73)' and add a fourth surface: 'JiraBackend.map_local_to_remote delegator (jira/backend.py:219) — accepts type_map and forwards into self.outbound', making the census four surfaces (Protocol + _JiraOutbound + JiraBackend delegator + DC).","tier":"LLM","validity":0.3333,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"no","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"yes","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"no","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"contradicts_reality","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}}],"impact_model_version":"plan-v5","material_fingerprint":"a7f326fc82f839b1","material_parts":{"children":["647ea2107ca5072f",0],"description":["414b109b8a7cc0fa",7924],"description_boxes":["7668d2cd32a37eb4",11],"file_impact":["3794734c916b19e1",17],"ticket_id":["d8a52704e3e7d462",19]},"metrics":{"cache_read_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"claim_path":"no-llm/no-network (structural; the fast claim check is a local HMAC verify)","det_ms":4069.0,"input_tokens":972612,"llm_calls":29,"llm_ms":263008.2,"output_tokens":28392,"precheck":{"cited_anchor_warning":false},"total_ms":275771.4,"verify_requests":19},"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-sonnet-4-6","provider_provenance":{"candidates":["bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-sonnet-4-6","anthropic:claude-sonnet-4-6"],"capabilities":{"native_structured_output":true,"prompt_cache_style":"none","supports_temperature":true,"supports_thinking":true,"web_access":"off"},"endpoint_host":null,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-sonnet-4-6","provider":"bedrock","ran_model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-sonnet-4-6","region":"us-east-1","region_source":"repo-config","tier":"first_class"},"regver":"aa61189569d34126","review_phase":"planning","reviewed_related_material":[{"canonical_id":"bfe7-0900-c3d1-4141","material_fingerprint":"2814cef81e53ef63","role":"prerequisite"},{"canonical_id":"f1bc-75f6-ed8c-472f","material_fingerprint":"4b7913db7eca6f42","role":"prerequisite"}],"runner":"pydantic_ai","schema":"plan_re